Q: Long breadcrumb should be right-aligned when scrolled A: <p>We can fake “start scrolled to end” using <code>direction: rtl</code>.</p>
<p>This makes the scroll container naturally start from the right edge.</p>
<p>Then we reset text direction inside items.</p>
<h2>Your final code will look like this</h2>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>body {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

.container {
  border: 2px solid #333;
  padding: 20px;
  width: 320px;
  resize: horizontal;
  overflow: auto;
}

/* Breadcrumb container */
.breadcrumb-list {
  display: flex;
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0.5em;
  margin: 0 0 2em 0;
  gap: 0.5em;
  overflow-x: auto;

  /* 👇 Magic trick */
  direction: rtl;
}

/* Reset text direction */
.breadcrumb-list li {
  white-space: nowrap;
  direction: ltr;
}

/* Separator */
.breadcrumb-list li:not(:first-child)::before {
  content: &quot;|&quot;;
  margin: 0 0.5em;
  color: #999;
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;

  &lt;h3&gt;Normal (fits → looks normal)&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;ul class=&quot;breadcrumb-list&quot;&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;My Account&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;

  &lt;h3&gt;Overflow → starts from the end&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;ul class=&quot;breadcrumb-list&quot;&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Adidas Hoodie XL&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Sweatshirts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Clothes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Men&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
