Q: Input type=date appears blank on android A: <p>An alternative would be to set the current time as a &quot;placeholder&quot; (that is to &quot;prefill&quot; the <code>value</code> attribute with the current time) with JavaScript, like so:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;input type="date" id="e"&gt;
&lt;script&gt;
  document.getElementById('e').value = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];
&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
